## MEMORANDUM OF OBJECTS AND REASONS

## Statement of objects and reasons

The principal object of the Bill is to provide for the merger of the Export Processing Zones Authority and Special Economic Zones Authority in order to promote and facilitate global and local investors.

Part I (Clauses 1 — 3) of the Bill provides for the preliminary provisions including the short title of the Bill, interpretation of the terms used in the Bill and the objects and application of the Bill.

Part II (Clauses 4 — 23) of the Bill contains administrative provisions. It establishes the Authority which will be a successor of the merger between Export Processing Zones Authority and Special Economic Zones Authority and outlines its functions. It provides for the Board of the Authority, its functions, powers, qualifications of members and appointment of the Chief Executive Officer, Corporation Secretary and the staff of the Authority.

Part III (Clauses 24—25) of the Bill provides for the declaration of special economic zones and the criteria for designing special economic zones.

Part IV (Clauses 26—30) of the Bill provides for the establishment of the Export processing zones. It provides for the declaration and export processing zones. It provides for the revocation of a declaration of an export processing zone, activities permitted within an export processing zone and prohibited activities within export processing zone.

Part V (Clause 31—35) of the Bill provides for operations within a special economic zone and an export processing zone. It provides for goods and services considered as exported and goods and services considered as imported. It also provides for goods and services within a special economic zone and export processing zone. It also provides for removal of goods from special economic zones and export processing zone and facilities within a special economic and export processing zone.

Part VI (Clauses 36—45) of the Bill provides for licensing. It states the procedure for licenses, notices of licenses issued to Kenya Revenue Authority, suspension of licenses and revocation of licenses. The receipts and payment of special economic zone and export processing zone enterprises. It provides for the register of licenses, issuance of the Kenya Economic Zones Service Permit, suspension of the Kenya Economic Zones Service Permit, revocation of the Kenya Economic Zones Service Permit and the register of permits.

Part VII (Clauses 46—54) of the Bill provides for the Special Economic Zones and Export Processing Zones Developers, Operators and Enterprises. It contains the special economic zone developers and operators, special economic zones enterprises, right and obligations of special economic zone developers and operators and export processing zone developer. It also provides for the obligations of an export processing zone developer, export processing zone enterprise, obligations of an export processing zone enterprise, rights of special economic zone and export processing zone enterprise. It also provides for the rights of special economic zone and export processing zone enterprises, developers and operators.

Part VIII (Clause 55) of the Bill provides for the Kenya Economic Zones Service Provider.

Part IX (Clauses 56—62) of the Bill provides for financial provisions. It provides for funds of the Authority, financial year, annual estimates, account and audits, annual report, bank account and investment of funds.

Part X (Clauses 63—66) of the Bill provides for miscellaneous provisions. It contains provisions for exemption from stamp duty, data protection, disputes and appeals.

Part XI (Clause 67) of the Bill provides for general penalty.

Part XII (Clause 68) of the Bill provides for the delegated powers of the Cabinet Secretary to make Regulations under the Act.

Part XIII— (Clause 69—70) of the Bill provides for the transitional provisions which include repeals and transition.

The First Schedule of the Bill contains provisions as to the conduct of business and affairs of the Board.

Statement on the delegation of legislative powers and limitation of

fundamental rights and freedoms

The Bill delegates legislative powers to the Cabinet Secretary but does not limit fundamental rights and freedoms.

Statement as to whether the Bill concerns county governments

The Bill does not concern county governments in terms of Article 110(1)(a) of the Constitution as it does not contain provisions affecting the functions and powers of the county governments set out in the Fourth Schedule to the Constitution. Paragraph 9 of the Fourth schedule to the Constitution provides that national economic policy and planning is a national government function.

Statement as to whether the Bill is a money Bill within the meaning of Article 114 of the Constitution

The Bill is a money Bill for purposes of Article 114 of the Constitution as the enactment of this Bill may occasion additional expenditure of public funds.

